  <running_head>Carolum Rupifortem.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">ejufmodi, quod effent de Synedrio, &amp;</l>
    <l n="2">in eo haberent jus suffragii, adeoque</l>
    <l n="3">acerrimi vindices Poteftatis Ecclefiasti-</l>
    <l n="4">cæ, &amp; in ea sententia se in synodo aut</l>
    <l n="5">syncdrio considentes nullo jure obnox-</l>
    <l n="6">ios esse reddendis rationibus Magi-</l>
    <l n="7">stratui. Non erit alienum hos &amp; illos</l>
    <l n="8">audire loquentes.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Agmen de illis qui synedria &amp; syno-</l>
    <l n="10">dos, Magistratus subjiciunt judicio,</l>
    <l n="11">ducat Marefius. Is loco <i>16 loc. com.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">sic decurtat authoritatem synodorum</l>
    <l n="13">&amp; canonum, ut dicat pastores in sy-</l>
    <l n="14">nodo non esse judices, sed referre doc-</l>
    <l n="15">tores prudentes &amp; peritos, non alia</l>
    <l n="16">præditos authoritate in populum fide-</l>
    <l n="17">lem, quam Medicos in ægros, quorum</l>
    <l n="18">canones, non obligant, nisi quatenus</l>
    <l n="19">concordare videntur cum sacro codice.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Rivetus in Decalogum, <i>Ministri</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>quatenus Ministri, sunt summi Magi-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>stratus subditi; cur autem à subditis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>&amp; eorum judicio, non liceat provocare</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>ad summum Magistratum? Et cur su-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>premo Magistratui judicia subditorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>non liceat recognoscere: si bona, rata habere,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>si mala abolere?</i>
    </l>
